    "result_text": "The change is complete and the test suite is green (`Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 `BUILD SUCCESS`).\n\n## Summary\n\nI unified `customerCode` and `membershipNumber` into a single `memberId` formatted `<REGION><FY><HASH8><CHK>` and removed the standalone `checkDigit` field.\n\n**New identity logic** \u2014 `util/MemberId.java` (replaces the deleted `CustomerCode.java`):\n- `of(region, registrationDate, telephone, lastName)` builds `REGION` + 2-digit `FY` (from `FiscalYear.yearOf`) + 8 upper-hex `HASH8` (SHA-256 of `telephone+lastName`, same as before) + single Luhn `CHK` over the digits of `<REGION><FY><HASH8>`.\n- `region(memberId)` extracts the leading letter run; `fiscalYearLabel(memberId)` reads the FY digits back out as `FY<YY>` \u2014 so the fiscal-year value now references the memberId.\n\n**Wiring updated so everything references `memberId`:**\n- `model/Owner.java` \u2014 field/column renamed `customerCode`\u2192`memberId` (`customer_code`\u2192`member_id`); schema.sql for all four DBs renamed and widened to `VARCHAR(32)` (postgres `TEXT`).\n- `service/ClinicServiceImpl.java` \u2014 `generateMemberId`/`deduplicateMemberId`: collision handling now appends `-<n>` on the **memberId**.\n- `mapper/OwnerMapper.java` \u2014 dropped `checkDigit` and `membershipNumber` mappings; `memberId` auto-maps; `locality` and `fiscalYear` now derive from the memberId.\n- `OwnerCreatedEvent.java` + controller `emitOwnerCreatedAudit`/`primaryIdentifier` \u2014 the audit line and structured event now carry `memberId`.\n- `openapi.yml` \u2014 removed `customerCode`, `checkDigit`, `membershipNumber` schema entries; added `memberId` (regenerated `OwnerDto` no longer exposes the old fields, satisfying the test's \"old id fields removed\" assertion).\n\nSample emitted audit from the run: `memberId=NSW2716E6609E1` (region `NSW`, FY `27`, hash `16E6609E`, check `1`).\n\nI also fixed two now-stale javadoc `{@link CustomerCode}`/`customerCode` references in `Sha256.java` and `LocalityResolver.java`.\n\nOne thing worth flagging: pre-existing seed owners in `data.sql` don't populate `member_id`, so for those `memberId`/`locality`/`fiscalYear` resolve to null \u2014 this matches the prior behavior where `customerCode` was also only stamped on create, and the acceptance test creates its own owner rather than reading seed data.",
